  "description": "Transition SYMMETRY document-invariant contract (accept/reject parity) for one cut between clip A (outgoing) and clip B (incoming) on a 30fps video track. Rules measured together: (1) adjacency — a transition edge needs a touching media-clip neighbour (gapUs > 0 breaks it); (2) symmetry — A.transitionOut and B.transitionIn must BOTH exist and be deep-equal (type + durationUs); (3) duration — D must sit on the project frame grid as an EVEN frame count >= 2, and D*2 must not exceed the shorter neighbour's timeline duration; (4) HEAD handle — B needs sourceInUs >= roundHalfUp(halfUs * B.rate) where halfUs is the FRAME-LEDGER half (frameToUs(dFrames/2)), and a still-image B (bStill) is exempt because -loop 1 has no time axis. Consumed by packages/timeline-schema/tests/invariants.test.ts (zod validateTimelineDoc WITHOUT assetDurations — the TAIL handle needs asset durations, the C# referee ExportCompiler.Validate cannot see them either, so it stays out of this file) and backend/tests/VideoEdit.UnitTests/TransitionSymmetryParityTests.cs. Clip construction per case: A starts at 0 with duration aDurationUs, sourceIn 0, sourceOut = aDurationUs * aRate; B starts at aDurationUs + gapUs with duration bDurationUs, sourceIn bSourceInUs, sourceOut = bSourceInUs + bDurationUs * bRate (rates are 1 or 2 so the duration formula holds exactly); bStill replaces B with an image clip (sourceIn 0, sourceOut = duration). All starts/edges sit on the 30fps grid; every invalid case keeps the other rules satisfied so it isolates exactly one rule. The half-frame-ledger-boundary case is the measured divergence this family existed for: for D = 14 frames (466667us) the compiler's half is frameToUs(7) = 233333us while naive roundHalfUp(D/2) is 233334us — the zod gate used to demand 1us MORE handle than the renderer and rejected a document the renderer accepts; invariants.ts now derives the half from the frame ledger. This closes the 'gecis simetrisi' family of the document-invariant parity gap recorded in docs/backlog.md (14. tur, M3 sinifi).",
